+              <li><strong>Legal compliance:</strong> recordkeeping and lawful requests.</li>
+            </ul>
+
+            <h2 id="when-we-disclose-personal-information" class="font-heading text-2xl">
+              When we disclose personal information
+            </h2>
+            <p>We don’t sell your personal information. We disclose only as needed to:</p>
+            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
+              <li>
+                <strong>Service providers:</strong> hosting, payment processing, shipping/couriers,
+                email/support tools, and <strong>analytics (Google Analytics)</strong>. Providers
+                receive only what’s necessary and must use it securely for our purposes.
+              </li>
+              <li>
+                <strong>Professional advisers:</strong> accountants, auditors, insurers, lawyers.
+              </li>
+              <li>
+                <strong>Legal/regulatory:</strong> where required by law or to protect
+                rights/safety.
+              </li>
+              <li>
+                <strong>Business change:</strong> if we undergo a sale/restructure, customer data
+                may transfer under the same protections.
+              </li>
+            </ul>
+
+            <h2 id="overseas-disclosures-app-8" class="font-heading text-2xl">
+              Overseas disclosures (APP 8)
+            </h2>
+            <p>
+              Some providers may store or access data from outside Australia (e.g.,
+              cloud/analytics).
+              <strong>In particular, we use Google Analytics provided by Google LLC (USA)</strong>
+              to understand website usage. We take reasonable steps so recipients protect it
+              consistently with the APPs (e.g., contractual and technical safeguards).
+            </p>
+
+            <h2 id="security-app-11" class="font-heading text-2xl">Security (APP 11)</h2>
+            <p>
+              We use administrative, technical and physical safeguards appropriate to the risk,
+              including TLS/SSL in transit, hardened hosting, access controls/least-privilege, and
+              periodic reviews. No system is 100% secure; if a data incident occurs, we’ll act
+              promptly.
+            </p>
+
+            <h3 id="data-breaches-voluntary" class="font-medium">Data breaches (voluntary)</h3>
+            <p>
+              Although many small businesses are exempt from the Notifiable Data Breaches scheme, we
+              aim to act consistently with its principles. If we suspect a breach likely to result
+              in <strong>serious harm</strong>, we will promptly assess and, where appropriate,
+              <strong>notify affected individuals</strong>,
+              <strong>provide guidance on protective steps</strong>, and
+              <strong>consider notifying the OAIC</strong>.
+            </p>
+
